  "description": "A sietch binds its people to shared stores, labor and the stone that shelters them. Its survival depends on careful use of water and the ability to leave refuge when work demands it.\n\nFremen equipment and skills reflect that life: stillsuits conserve moisture, sandwalking quiets movement, and blades serve where shield emissions would be dangerous.",
